[Medium] Fail closed for credentialed CORS/Socket.IO origins on gello_rana #29
Open
Open
[\[Medium\] Fail closed for credentialed CORS/Socket.IO origins on gello_rana](https://github.com/MAKASA-LABORATORY/BCIIS-Server/issues/29#top)#29
Description
[maxangelo987](https://github.com/maxangelo987)
opened [2w ago](https://github.com/MAKASA-LABORATORY/BCIIS-Server/issues/29#issue-5291477066)
Collaborative-only audit finding
Branch reviewed: gello_rana @ bcb8d936.
Server/server.js enables credentialed cross-origin requests but falls back to permissive origins when environment configuration is absent:
HTTP CORS uses origin: process.env.CORS_ORIGIN || true with credentials: true, which reflects/accepts arbitrary browser origins when CORS_ORIGIN is missing.
Socket.IO uses origin: process.env.SOCKET_IO_ORIGIN || '*' with credentials: true, similarly failing open when the allowlist is not configured.
The global error handler also returns err.message to clients in production; internal errors should be logged server-side while production clients receive a generic message.
This branch does add useful controls—Helmet, compression, request IDs, rate limiting, JWT-secret fail-fast checks, timeouts, and graceful shutdown. Preserve those improvements while correcting the configuration defaults.
Required remediation
Fail closed in non-development environments when allowed origins are missing; parse an explicit allowlist and reject non-matching origins.
Apply the same explicit allowlist policy to Socket.IO; do not use * with credentials.
Keep development localhost origins explicit rather than using broad reflection as a production fallback.
Return generic 5xx client messages in production; retain detailed errors only in server logs/development diagnostics.
Add tests proving an allowed origin succeeds, an unlisted origin is rejected, missing production allowlist prevents insecure startup or requests, and Socket.IO follows the same policy.
Branch naming/process note
gello_rana is contributor-oriented rather than task-oriented. Do not rename this branch automatically, but use task/module names for future work, e.g. fix/cors-allowlist, security/socket-origin-policy, or the actual assigned module.
