[Critical][Jamesnew] Admin application review/approval routes are unauthenticated #31
Open
Open
[\[Critical\]\[Jamesnew\] Admin application review/approval routes are unauthenticated](https://github.com/MAKASA-LABORATORY/BCIIS-Server/issues/31#top)#31
Description
[maxangelo987](https://github.com/maxangelo987)
opened [2w ago](https://github.com/MAKASA-LABORATORY/BCIIS-Server/issues/31#issue-5294226736)
Scope
Backlog audit of source-bearing branch Jamesnew at 6619dfe3 (May 10, 2026). This is a branch-specific finding and should not be treated as a regression on current main unless the same code is merged there.
Critical — admin application review and approval are reachable without authentication/authorization
Server/server.js mounts /admin-applications directly with no global auth guard. In Server/routes/admin_applications.routes.js, the following routes have no authentication/role middleware:
GET /pending
GET /all
GET /:id
PUT /:id/approve
PUT /:id/reject
The approve/reject handlers also trust reviewedBy from the request body instead of deriving the reviewer from a verified server-side principal. If this branch is deployed/reused, an unauthenticated caller can enumerate pending admin applications and attempt to approve/reject them, while spoofing the reviewer identifier.
Medium — raw internal errors are returned to clients
Several handlers interpolate err.message into 500 responses. Keep detailed DB/runtime diagnostics in restricted logs and return generic production errors.
Positive control
The reviewed database operations use parameterized stored-procedure calls (CALL ... with placeholder arrays). Preserve that SP-only pattern.
Required remediation
Require a server-verifiable authenticated session/JWT on all admin-application review routes.
Enforce an explicit privileged reviewer role server-side before list/read/approve/reject operations.
Derive reviewedBy from the authenticated principal; never accept it as caller-authoritative input.
Return only the minimum application fields required for review and avoid leaking password hashes or other sensitive columns from stored procedures.
Replace raw err.message client responses with sanitized errors.
Add negative tests for anonymous access, wrong-role access, spoofed reviewer IDs, repeated processing, and cross-account/admin privilege escalation.
Branch naming process warning
Jamesnew is personal/vague and does not identify the task or module. Do not rename history destructively; for future work use a task-oriented name such as fix/admin-application-authz or feature/admin-application-review.
Suggested course alignment
DSA W2 — ADTs/data flow/backend operations: document request → authentication → role authorization → validation → parameterized stored procedure → sanitized response, with negative tests as evidence.
No application source, source branch, PR state, or merge history was modified by this audit.


