The dev branch mounts /farmers with only the search rate limiter. The farmer router itself has no authentication or authorization middleware, yet it exposes farmer listing/search and permits create, update, delete, and bulk-delete operations by caller-supplied IDs/body data.
The implementation does use parameterized stored-procedure calls and transactions for the relational operations, which is positive and should be preserved. However, rate limiting is not an authorization control. The current route surface permits anonymous access to sensitive farmer/profile information and anonymous mutation/deletion if the branch is deployed or otherwise reachable.
The handlers also return raw err.message values in 500 responses, which can disclose database/runtime details.
Required remediation
Require server-verifiable authentication before farmer/profile reads and mutations.
