Do not trust caller-selected record IDs as authorization. Derive allowed scope from the verified session/token and enforce it server-side.
Preserve the existing parameterized stored-procedure boundary and transaction handling.
Replace raw database/runtime error messages in client responses with generic production-safe messages; retain diagnostics only in restricted server logs.
Add tests covering anonymous access (401), authenticated-but-unauthorized access (403), authorized reads/mutations, cross-scope ID attempts, bulk-delete authorization, transaction rollback, and sanitized failures.
Branch naming process warning
dev is too generic for active implementation work. Do not rename or rewrite this branch as part of remediation, but future work should use task-oriented names such as fix/farmer-route-authz, feature/farmer-directory-rbac, or the actual assigned module/task.
No secret values or application records are reproduced in this issue.


