Medium — newly added map API router is unreachable
The branch adds Server/routes/maps.routes.js with parameterized stored-procedure endpoints for municipality/Bohol land suitability and sampling sites, including save/delete operations. However, the reviewed Server/server.js neither imports nor mounts this router, so those endpoints are unreachable and cannot be integration-tested through the application.
Before mounting it, add explicit authentication/RBAC for every mutation, decide/document whether reads are intentionally public, validate IDs/coordinates/GeoJSON inputs, and sanitize err.message responses. Preserve the current parameterized CALL sp_* pattern.
Required remediation
Require a server-verifiable session/JWT before sensitive profile reads and all profile mutations.
Apply least-privilege RBAC/ownership/scope checks; do not treat caller-selected IDs as authorization.
Keep profile and maps runtime relational operations parameterized and stored-procedure-only.
Sanitize client errors and avoid logging/reproducing personal profile data.
If the map module is intended for this lineage, explicitly mount it after authentication/authorization is defined and add route-level integration tests.
Add negative tests for anonymous/wrong-role/cross-scope profile operations and unauthorized map mutations, plus successful authorized SP-backed paths.
Branch naming/process warning
RonoloJ_bagoR is contributor-oriented and does not identify the task/module. Do not rename/rewrite this historical branch solely for the audit. For future work, use task-aligned names such as fix/profile-access-control, feature/map-land-suitability-api, or the actual assigned task.
Suggested DSA course task
Suggested DSA course task — W2 ADTs/data flow/backend operations; W16 testing/evidence: document and test request → authenticated principal → authorization → validation → parameterized SP → sanitized response, with integration evidence for the map router if it is retained.
No application source, branch state, PR state, or deployment was modified by this audit. No secret values or personal records are reproduced here.
